++{"citation_id": "cite-20261024-006", "issue": 844, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which domain must the slice's new capability sit in?", "answer": "None is needed: a capability with an empty domain is ready, with a warning only; no domain shelf holds Garura's field (routing-result.json).", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-24T03:59:51Z", "trace": [{"asked": "is a capability with no domain ready", "found": "an empty domain is ready, with the warning 'has no domain yet'", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/features/fn-724/feature.md", "start": 20, "end": 21, "fingerprint": "sha256:4fdd6fefe124ba86804cbd9be67ca4e768810f68637e97e1eaaf9739fcd0fdb0", "text": "- A capability with an empty `domain`, or with a domain id that is not in the spine, is also ready. The check adds the warning \"has no domain yet\" or \"is not in the spine\". It never sets `workable` to false for this reason.\n- A node with no intent, or with only proposed or dropped intents, is not ready. The check keeps it exactly as written. The check stops work on it, never the write that made it.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 17, "end": 24, "text": "## Rules & behavior\n- A capability is ready when at least one business intent in its `intents` is confirmed or met, and none of its needs is open. A met intent counts, because it was confirmed first. Work that keeps it met is still wanted.\n- A feature is ready when its capability is ready and none of its own needs is open. The capability can be ready through its own confirmed intent or through the intent of the feature.\n- A capability with an empty `domain`, or with a domain id that is not in the spine, is also ready. The check adds the warning \"has no domain yet\" or \"is not in the spine\". It never sets `workable` to false for this reason.\n- A node with no intent, or with only proposed or dropped intents, is not ready. The check keeps it exactly as written. The check stops work on it, never the write that made it.\n- A missing business intent page counts as not confirmed. Thus a link to an intent that nobody wrote never makes a node ready.\n- A need that is not in the done list is open. An open need makes the node blocked and not ready, and the reason names what the node waits for. Without a done list, the check shows the needs, but they do not change the answer.\n- A feature whose capability is not in the spine is not ready, because it has no capability to be ready through."}}}], "from_update": null}
